<title>USA: Banner says Delta deal worth up to $150 mln.</title>
<headline>Banner says Delta deal worth up to $150 mln.</headline>
<dateline>FT. LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Solair, a unit of Banner Aerospace said Thursday that it has signed a memorandum of understanding with Delta Air Lines Inc  to be Delta's sole source supplier of airframe material such as rotables, repairables and expendables, from the surplus market.</p>
<p>The company said the deal, which is subject to a definitive agreement, could generate $150 million in revenues over the next three years.</p>
<p>Solair also said that it plans to hire additional support staff in its Lakeland, Fla. and Atlanta facilities as a result of the agreemnt.</p>
